  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Place a medium bowl (preferably metal) in the freezer to chill. (If space is limited, place in the refrigerator.)",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash, dry, and cut off skin from pineapple; quarter, core, and medium dice the flesh. Divide pineapple between glasses or jars. (Stemless wine glasses work great for this.)",
      "secondary_message": "1 small pineapple"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash and dry the oranges. Cut off skin and white pith from each orange, slice between the membranes to release segments, then cut into bite-sized pieces. Add to the glasses with the pineapple and set aside.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Remove bowl from the freezer. Pour cold cream, sugar, and vanilla into the bowl.",
      "secondary_message": "237 ml heavy whipping cream\n2 tsp granulated sugar\n½ tsp vanilla extract"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Use a whisk (or hand blender) to beat the cream vigorously, until medium-soft peaks form, about 3 minutes if whisking. (When you pull the whisk out of the bowl, the cream should hold its shape, with a peak that curls over slightly.)\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "To serve, top fruit parfaits with whipped cream and sprinkle with candy corn. Enjoy!",
      "secondary_message": "⅛ cup candy corn"
    }
  ],
